  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "EDH",
      "text": "Everything DeepSeek Harness — one plugin, one master switch, a feature per row."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "| Feature | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `retry` | Retries a failed model request inside the same turn, with no attempt limit |\n| `edit` | Adds a pencil to every user message: forks the Session just before it and puts the text back in the composer |\n| `btw` | `/btw` and `/side` open a side chat: a fork of this conversation, shown beside it in the right-hand pane |\n| `export` | Downloads the Session as a Markdown document |\n| `update` | Updates EDH itself from its published repo, from EDH's page in Plugin Manager, and reloads the new browser half in place |\n| `mcp` | Connects MCP servers from a settings page — no Cordis config — and gives their tools to the model as it goes |\n| `remote` | Opens the same Web GUI on a phone over the LAN, behind a login page and a username and password you set |\n| `usage` | Shows where your tokens went: totals, per model and per day across every Session, with streaks and peaks |\n| `mobile` | Serves the web app manifest, so a phone can add the GUI to its home screen and open it without browser chrome |\n| `notify` | Serves a curated few of the real Windows sound files, so a notification plays the sound you already know |\n| `search` | Full-text search acros"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "A switch in the conversation header turns them all on or off together."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "EDH is a Harness bundle: the package carries a `dsh.bundle.patch`, which adds its Loader\nrows. Install it like any other bundle — `\"@moreweb/edh\": \"link:/path/to/EDH\"`, or the\npacked tarball — then enable the rows you want in Plugin Manager."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
